   "text": {
    "L1": "A timeline helps us place events in order, from earlier to later.",
    "L2": "BCE years count backwards, so 500 BCE is earlier than 100 BCE. The bigger BCE number is farther back.",
    "L3": "CE years count up from 1 CE. There is no year 0: 1 BCE is followed directly by 1 CE.",
    "L4": "For example, 2600 BCE comes before 268 BCE, and 1947 CE comes later on the timeline.",
    "L5": "A decade is 10 years, a century is 100 years, and a millennium is 1,000 years.",
    "L6": "Historians use remains, inscriptions, written texts, and oral traditions as sources.",
    "L7": "They cross-check many sources because one source can be incomplete or show only one point of view.",
    "L8": "Now put these dates in order from earliest to latest."
   },
